Package: ripgrep
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armhf
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: recursively searches directories for a regex pattern
 ripgrep is a line-oriented search tool that recursively searches the current
 directory for a regex pattern while respecting your gitignore rules and
 automatically skipping hidden files/directories and binary files (smart
 filtering). ripgrep is similar to other popular search tools like The Silver
 Searcher, ack and grep.
 .
 ripgrep is generally faster than both The Silver Searcher and GNU grep. It
 defaults to recursive directory search and won't search files ignored by your
 `.gitignore` files. Use ripgrep if you like speed, filtering by default, fewer
 bugs, and Unicode support.
 .
 This package repackages the statically linked musl binary published upstream.
 PCRE2 is compiled in, so unlike the Debian archive build it needs no shared
 libraries at runtime.
